# this note is from previous iCE40 projects
iCE40 open-drain implementation:
    both SCL and SDA must use SB_IO primitives (not assign statements)
    use single oe signal: oe=1 drives LOW, oe=0 releases to pull-up
    add _CMD and _WAIT states that detect falling edge of i2c_busy to ensure each command completes before the next

    SB_IO #(
        .PIN_TYPE(6'b101001),
        .PULLUP(1'b0)
    ) scl_io (
        .PACKAGE_PIN(scl),
        .OUTPUT_CLK(clk),
        .OUTPUT_ENABLE(scl_oe),
        .D_OUT_0(1'b0),
        .D_IN_0()
    );


when all the steps have been verified, create a comprehensive README.md

● I2C PRD Directives                                                            
                                                                                
  1. Command-based interface - Separate START/WRITE/READ/STOP commands, not     
  single-transaction                                                            
  2. SB_IO inside i2c_master - Not in top.v                                     
  3. seen_busy pattern - if (busy) seen_busy<=1; else if (seen_busy) next_state;
  4. 100 kHz timing - HALF_PERIOD=60, sample ACK at end of HIGH period          



